From 436f59616d73a217e241e6f7faa01a29fab31ed6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Miroslav=20Mr=C3=A1z?= <miroslav.mraz@techmania.cz>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 00:19:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH v1 2/2] media: i2c: add Samsung S5K3L6XX sensor driver
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add a V4L2 sub-device driver for the Samsung S5K3L6XX, a 13MP CMOS image
sensor on a 4-lane MIPI CSI-2 D-PHY interface. It is the ultra-wide
camera of the Samsung Galaxy A52 4G (a52q, SM7125).

The driver exposes a 4000x3000 mode and a 2x2-binned 2000x1500 mode at
30 fps with exposure, analogue gain, vblank/hblank and test-pattern
controls. The register tables were decoded from the vendor CamX sensor
module.

Based on the S5K3L6XX driver by Martin Kepplinger and Dorota
Czaplejewicz (Purism SPC).

Signed-off-by: Miroslav Mráz <miroslav.mraz@techmania.cz>
